elve volunteers used, on average, a little under half of it. The protection you get does not fall in a straight line with the amount, but it does fall: half the sunscreen gives you a good deal less than half the number on the front."}</p><figure className={"article-wide grid grid-cols-[minmax(0,5fr)_minmax(0,4fr)] [align-items:end] gap-6 my-12 max-md:grid-cols-1"}><img className={"w-full aspect-[4/3] object-cover rounded-(--custom-stage-r)"} src={"https://draftmango.com/draftmango/assets/media/placeholder/720x900.svg"} alt={"A swipe of white sunscreen on sand-coloured stone under dappled sun"} width={"720"} height={"900"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /><figcaption className={"p-6 text-[1rem] leading-[1.55] bg-(--custom-band) rounded-(--custom-r)"}><strong>{"Two finger-lengths"}</strong>{" for face and neck, about 1.25 ml. It looks like a lot the first week; by the third it is habit."}</figcaption></figure><h2 className={"font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em]"}>{"How to get there without feeling greasy"}</h2><ol><li><strong>{"Apply in two layers."}</strong>{" One finger-length, spread it, wait a minute, then the second. Two thin layers sit better than one thick one."}</li><li className={"mt-2.5"}><strong>{"Make it your moisturiser."}</strong>{" A fluid like Sheer Daylight SPF 50 hydrates enough for most skin; drop the cream underneath on oily days."}</li><li className={"mt-2.5"}><strong>{"Remember the edges."}</strong>{" Hairline, ears, the sides of the neck: the places most often missed and most often burnt."}</li></ol><table className={"custom-article-table w-full text-[1rem]"}><caption className={"mb-3 text-[0.9375rem] font-semibold text-left text-text"}>{"How much, where (at 2 mg per square centimetre)"}</caption><thead><tr><th className={"text-[0.875rem] font-semibold text-muted bg-(--custom-band)"} scope={"col"}>{"Area"}</th><th className={"text-[0.875rem] font-semibold text-muted bg-(--custom-band)"} scope={"col"}>{"Amount"}</th><th className={"text-[0.875r